Rule Language

Conditions

Conditions support various operators:

```json
{
  "operator": "and",
  "left_operand": [
    {
      "operator": "gte",
      "left_operand": "$age",
      "right_operand": 18
    },
    {
      "operator": "lt",
      "left_operand": "$income",
      "right_operand": 100000
    }
  ]
}
```

Thresholds

Define and check thresholds:

```python
thresholds = {
    "income": {"max": 75000, "warning": 65000},
    "age": {"min": 18, "max": 65}
}

results = engine.check_thresholds("rule-set-id", values, thresholds)
```

API Reference

REST API

Start the API server:

```bash
uvicorn gitdigital.api.main:app --reload
```

Available endpoints:

· POST /api/v1/policies - Load a policy
· GET /api/v1/policies/{policy_id} - Get policy details
· POST /api/v1/policies/{policy_id}/evaluate - Evaluate eligibility
· POST /api/v1/compliance/check - Check compliance

Python API

```python
from gitdigital import PolicyEngine, PolicyDSL

# Create engine
engine = PolicyEngine(mode="strict", cache_enabled=True)

# Load policy
policy = engine.load_policy(policy_data, format="json")

# Evaluate
decision = engine.evaluate_eligibility(policy_id, applicant_data)

# Check thresholds
threshold_results = engine.check_thresholds(
    rule_set_id, 
    values, 
    thresholds
)
```

